        "abstract": "The Method of Moments Body of Revolution technique is used to predict radiation from asymmetrically excited apertures on a class of perfectly conducting rotationally symmetric structures. This paper briefly outlines the theoretical basis of the method, proposes some corrections to previous work on the subject and presents a new formulation for a cosinusoidal aperture distribution. Results computed using the method are compared with measured results (from the literature) for the pitch and roll plane patterns of an aperture on a cone-sphere. Results are also compared with the roll plane patterns computed using the geometrical theory of diffraction for axial slots on a cylinder, and with measured roll plane patterns for this case. Numerical convergence of the method is discussed.",
