        "abstract": "The finite element method is used to design an etched microstrip balun for transforming a 100 ohm balanced impedance to a 50 ohm unbalanced coaxial cable. Design curves for determining the required impedances along the balun are presented. An etched balun was incorporated into a planar Archimedes spiral antenna and the performance of this antenna is compared to that of a second spiral antenna fed by a tapered coaxial line balun. Examination of the VSWR, patterns, axial ratio, squint and gain shows that the performance of the two baluns is equivalent with the etched balun having superior squint properties.",
