        "abstract": "This paper introduces the concept that extremely fat monopole antennas (length-to-diameter ratio of about two) can be made to operate with VSWR less than 2:1 over a 3:1 frequency bandwidth at microwave frequencies. These monopole antennas exploit the physical dimensions of commonly used microwave coaxial connectors to reduce excess base capacitance. The body of revolution moment method is used to predict the elevation patterns of very fat cylindrical and conical monopoles mounted at the centre of finite circular ground planes. Excellent agreement is achieved between predicted and measured patterns.",
