        "abstract": "Results of a numerical analysis, using the finite element technique, on a polarizer designed for an S-band slotted waveguide array are presented. The polarizer consisted essentially of an array of waveguides of parallelogram cross-section, with the acute angle 45 degrees. The polarizer had poor axial ratio and the purpose of the analysis was to determine the parametric dependence of the axial ratio on the acute angle. The optimum value for the angle was found to be approximately 39 degrees. With the angle 45 degrees the predicted axial ratio was approximately 1 dB, assuming no phase error. Problems encountered with the finite element technique are also discussed.",
        "keywords": {
